  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Communities in Shan State to have sustainable livelihood away from illicit drugs cultivation through the nexus approach that addresses humanitarian needs, poverty reduction, and peacebuilding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the programme is to support the vulnerable communities in their transition towards licit economic activities by strengthening sustainable value chains under a Nexus-based approach (humanitarian, development, and peacebuilding).&#xb300;&#xccb4; &#xc791;&#xbb3c; &#xc7ac;&#xbc30; &#xbc0f; &#xac00;&#xce58;&#xc0ac;&#xc2ac; &#xac15;&#xd654;, &#xc9c0;&#xc5ed;&#xc0ac;&#xd68c;&#xc758; &#xb9c8;&#xc57d; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xb300;&#xc751; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9; &#xac15;&#xd654;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will focus on reinforcing existing value chains such as coffee, tea, and avocado, while expanding coverage to new areas vulnerable to illicit crop cultivation. Additionally, efforts will be directed towards identifying and supporting new value chains and developing drug use prevention strategies. This approach aims to comprehensively address humanitarian needs, reduce poverty, promote peacebuilding, and prevent drug use, contributing to enhanced community resilience and the creation of economic opportunities that enable farmers to disengage from illicit crops. It will also be better equipped communities to face economic, social, and environmental challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
